{"id": "EUVD-2026-86869", "enisaUuid": "2cf2a044-f5e0-3cbb-be85-c115bde2f96a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: honor forceuid/forcegid when mapping SIDs to uid/gid\n\nWhen the administrator mounts with forceuid or forcegid (uid=/gid=\nmount options), they expect all files to appear owned by the specified\nuser/group.  However, several code paths unconditionally called\nsid_to_id() to overwrite cf_uid/cf_gid with server-provided values,\nignoring the administrator's explicit override:\n\n  - smb311_posix_info_to_fattr() (stat via POSIX extensions)\n  - cifs_posix_to_fattr() (readdir via POSIX extensions)\n  - parse_sec_desc() (CIFS ACL ownership mapping)\n\nThis allowed an untrusted server to dictate local file ownership even\nwhen the mount was configured to force specific uid/gid values.\n\nFix all three call sites to check CIFS_MOUNT_OVERR_UID and\nCIFS_MOUNT_OVERR_GID before calling sid_to_id(), following the\nsame pattern already used by cifs_unix_basic_to_fattr() for unix\nextensions.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be6eccccec867c22d7c65fab4ea4e91ec3d5b8c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc35de451c128d399ad185d6269f8847e97cd1c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ac7a29691558bed18e2df1780636b8aa0fd13d5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1b74f8f8c1d13190b09fe623b729d36b7ac22a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/18a72975e9f35aadecc75b031f693f2d1f49308f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vg8h-339p-69c7", "CVE-2026-97561"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3bc10c47-ee42-32af-b2be-a51dc18636f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9409ae58e0759d010b347e7b19ebc90ab5d4b98f <e1b74f8f8c1d13190b09fe623b729d36b7ac22a8"}, {"id": "7cb2c3a9-ffe9-316d-8697-9a584448444e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9409ae58e0759d010b347e7b19ebc90ab5d4b98f <6ac7a29691558bed18e2df1780636b8aa0fd13d5"}, {"id": "7e1b3ccd-ed25-3c48-bc12-fbfc644d1398", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9409ae58e0759d010b347e7b19ebc90ab5d4b98f <18a72975e9f35aadecc75b031f693f2d1f49308f"}, {"id": "7e92a8e6-e2c9-3c47-b314-1063056ec0fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "99ce11dc-8189-3b79-907e-0991fb4d8775", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9409ae58e0759d010b347e7b19ebc90ab5d4b98f <bc35de451c128d399ad185d6269f8847e97cd1c9"}, {"id": "a3a00614-f0c3-3ef4-9efa-1f7e00a5a505", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "a46881d5-2582-3d76-a25a-b1ff0543f50e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ac8e779a-a5d0-389c-9a0e-02d1b166a363", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c6fe516f-9a92-3361-b6c0-ecfc16bc33cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.0"}, {"id": "c78d9f3d-d2db-310d-8b4e-504d83f6c87d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9409ae58e0759d010b347e7b19ebc90ab5d4b98f <be6eccccec867c22d7c65fab4ea4e91ec3d5b8c6"}, {"id": "cb67dd87-b71e-3e6c-8af8-f523b209abf3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "feb358f9-fafd-327a-88aa-9007bedd472a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8f736fa5-33c7-3499-8bf1-8ecb53699ad6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}